From: Ziia Shi <mkrsym1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Avoid infinite wait during process termination.

Backported from WineHQ commit e0e8166da6 (wine-11.1) without code
changes.

During process termination, threadpool callbacks can no longer finish, so a
wait on them never returns and the process hangs on exit. Normal waits while
the process runs are unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/threadpool.c b/dlls/ntdll/threadpool.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/threadpool.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/threadpool.c
@@ -2083,7 +2083,7 @@
     struct threadpool *pool = object->pool;
 
     RtlEnterCriticalSection( &pool->cs );
-    while (!object_is_finished( object, group_wait ))
+    while (!RtlDllShutdownInProgress() && !object_is_finished( object, group_wait ))
     {
         if (group_wait)
             RtlSleepConditionVariableCS( &object->group_finished_event, &pool->cs, NULL );
